### Nyaalkaran ERP SaaS POC - the R1 admin flow, step by step.
### Run in IntelliJ (HTTP Client) top to bottom. Each step stores ids and tokens for the next one.
### Access tokens live 5 minutes: re-run step 0 (or 12a) if a later request returns 401.
@host = http://localhost:8080
@kc = http://localhost:8180

### 0. Platform Super Admin token from the platform realm erp-platform (POC: password grant of platform-console)
POST {{kc}}/realms/erp-platform/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=platform-console&username=superadmin&password=change-me

> {% client.global.set("platformToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 1. Catalog: modules, bundles, dependencies, current monthly price list
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/catalog?period=MONTHLY
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 2. Create a company (DRAFT, race-safe CMP_n code, login code, realm name co-n)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "legalName": "Shivam Minerals Pvt Ltd", "superAdminEmail": "admin@shivam.test" }

> {% client.global.set("company", response.body.companyCode);
     client.global.set("realm", "co-" + response.body.companyCode.substring(4)); %}

### 3. Quote: CRM + Store (Store pulls its mandatory Account Book dependency), 8 users, 25 GiB
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "billingPeriod": "MONTHLY", "modules": ["crm", "store"], "users": 8, "storageGb": 25 }

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.order.id); %}

### 4. Confirm the order: amounts frozen, subscription created PENDING
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/orders/{{orderId}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 5. Trying to provision now is refused: SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_ACTIVE (full payment first, CD-07)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/provision
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 6. Record a cash payment (immediate) for part of the total
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/orders/{{orderId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "CASH", "amount": 500 }

### 7. Record a cheque for the rest (PENDING_VERIFICATION until cleared)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/orders/{{orderId}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "CHEQUE", "amount": 290, "instrumentRef": "CHQ-000123", "bankName": "SBI" }

> {% client.global.set("chequeId", response.body.payments[1].id); %}

### 8. The cheque cleared: 100 % verified -> invoice ISSUED_PAID, subscription ACTIVE, entitlements computed
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/payments/{{chequeId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 9. Provision: realm co-n + Company Super Admin, one DB per entitled module, Liquibase per tenant, buckets, caches
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/provision
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 10. Watch the job (re-run until COMPLETED)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/provisioning-jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 11. Everything the platform knows: subscriptions, entitlements, allowances, resources (IDP_REALM co-n VERIFIED), Redis
GET {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 12. The invited Company Super Admin "accepts the invitation" (no SMTP in the POC, CD-19).
###     Simulated with the operator's Keycloak admin login (admin/admin, Keycloak console only): set a password
###     and clear the required actions. 12-1: operator token, 12-2: find the user, 12-3: password, 12-4: actions.
POST {{kc}}/realms/master/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=admin-cli&username=admin&password=admin

> {% client.global.set("operatorToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 12-2
GET {{kc}}/admin/realms/{{realm}}/users?email=admin@shivam.test&exact=true
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}

> {% client.global.set("ownerId", response.body[0].id);
     client.global.set("ownerAccepted", JSON.stringify(Object.assign(response.body[0],
         { requiredActions: [], emailVerified: true }))); %}

### 12-3
PUT {{kc}}/admin/realms/{{realm}}/users/{{ownerId}}/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "password", "value": "Shivam-Owner-1", "temporary": false }

### 12-4
PUT {{kc}}/admin/realms/{{realm}}/users/{{ownerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{ownerAccepted}}

### 12a. Company token from the company realm co-n: iss = .../realms/co-n, tenant_id = CMP_n, COMPANY_SUPER_ADMIN
POST {{kc}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=erp-web&username=admin@shivam.test&password=Shivam-Owner-1

> {% client.global.set("companyToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 13. Business API as the company: the company comes only from the verified token
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tenant/crm/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{companyToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerCode": "C-001", "name": "Rajesh Traders", "email": "rajesh@traders.test" }

### 14. Which physical database served the request? (an X-Company-Code header would be ignored)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tenant/crm/_routing
Authorization: Bearer {{companyToken}}

### 15. A module the company did not buy -> 403 MODULE_NOT_ENTITLED
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tenant/asset/anything
Authorization: Bearer {{companyToken}}

### 16. A platform token on the tenant API -> 401 (platform identities never reach business routes)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tenant/crm/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 17. Suspend -> business API returns 403 COMPANY_SUSPENDED (data is kept; re-run 13/14 to see it)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "SUSPENDED", "reason": "demo" }

### 18. Reactivate
POST {{host}}/api/v1/platform/companies/{{company}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "ACTIVE", "reason": "demo over" }
